WEBVTT

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:12.870
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.700
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.500
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.080
"Mankind has gotten lazy since they created robots"
"and over time, robots have taken their place..."
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.410
"That would never happen! The outrageous
anime <i>RobiHachi</i>" "Heads I'm Tin, Tails You Lose"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.950
"That would never happen! The outrageous
anime <i>RobiHachi</i>" "Heads I'm Tin, Tails You Lose"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.290
Ow...

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.410
Ik...

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.000
...ku! Can't you warp out any gentler?!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.250
Ow!

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.000
That didn't hurt; you're a robot.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.950
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.290
Wait, why are you just out of the bath, too?

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.000
I couldn't help it. This ship is a clunker.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.160
Huh? Are you talking back to a human?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.910
That's right. Robots were originally
built to serve people.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.500
You guys disgust me.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.540
Oh, is that the 42nd stage
station world, Mulberry 7?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.580
Mulberry 7 is apparently famous for its clams.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.290
Hooray! Grilled clams!
Grilled clams! Grilled clams!

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.870
--Grilled clams! Grilled clams!
--Grilled clams! Grilled clams!

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.450
Hey! You guys, we are just about
out of fuel! We have to hurry and land!

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.870
What is going on here?

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.250
It's a land of robots.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.950
Don't cry, now... Don't cry, now...

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.120
Wow...

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.540
Yahoo!

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.950
Out of the way! Move it, move it!

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.290
Watch it, you bastard!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.950
Be careful!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.830
What's your problem? Lowlife living creatures!

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.330
What do you mean, "living creatures"?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.750
Shut up, you idiot!

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.080
I'm sorry. They don't know any better.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.750
You have to discipline your slaves!

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.040
Let's get going, Prince.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.500
They're nobody you need
to concern yourself with.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.160
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.790
They called him a prince?
I'll show him a prince. How arrogant.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.700
Princes and "so-and-so-the-seconds"
are never decent folk.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.290
Y-You don't say.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.620
Damn it! Let's get some clams and
head off to the next world right away.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.250
I'm afraid we can't do that.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.000
--Huh?
--Why not?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.500
Apparently, we made a mistake and
we didn't land on Mulberry 7. This is 8.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.160
--We did what?!
--We did what?!

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.580
Here on Mulberry 8, robots and
mechanical people are in charge.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.080
It's an "If you aren't a mecha,
you aren't a man" kind of world.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:21.000
And since you guys aren't mechas,
you won't be treated as people.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.580
Well, what is a mechanical person, anyway?

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.870
Do they naturally occur on this world?

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.290
Beats me. You guys might be able to
get mechanical bodies if you buy them.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.830
Don't be ridiculous!

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:37.450
Damn it! If you aren't a mecha, you aren't
a man? Then we'll be mecha, too!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.080
--Hizakuri Formation!
--Hizakuri Formation!

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:42.540
Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:18.620
Hizakuriger!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.370
Now they've got no room to complain!

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.330
Grilled clams! Grilled clams!

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.040
You're absolutely sure of it?

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.870
--Yes!
--Robby and the others landed on this world.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.290
All right, take us down.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.950
--Roger!
--Roger!

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.120
What the hell is this?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.000
There's nothing here but mechas and robots!

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:03.160
You're in my way, living creatures.
Move aside, now!

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.580
What was that?

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:05.540
No, don't, Mr. Yang!

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:06.410
This way!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.830
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.200
You don't seem to know
the rules here on this world.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.080
Ha! I <i>am </i>the rules--

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.790
The rules on Mulberry 8 are,
"If you aren't a mecha, you aren't a man."

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.290
A-All right.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.000
Walk off more to the side, there.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.080
Are you all right, Mr. Yang?

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.040
Damn.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.870
On this world, mechas are the rulers,

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:36.250
and people aren't allowed
to defy mecha-people.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.700
This mecha and mecha-people
business is a hassle.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.330
I'll just have to become a man-mecha!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.040
How do you like me, man-mecha style?

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.500
Impressive, Mr. Yang!

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.290
You don't look human!

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.870
Good.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.700
Out of my way, mecha-man!

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.910
What was that?

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:04.910
Wait, it seems like I've seen you before.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.160
What, you want a piece of me?!

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.830
Show me whether you're
a mecha-man, or a mecha-sissy!

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.540
--Sir! Sir!
--Sir! Sir!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.000
<i>You </i>walk off more to the side!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.040
Why, you...!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.750
How dare you hurt him!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.500
Shing! Rub-rub.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:30.330
I was going to hire the man you
just defeated to be my bodyguard.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:34.790
What do you say? Would you be
my bodyguard instead of him?

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.290
What?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:40.370
Shing! I am one of the rulers of this world,

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.370
the Mecha-Count of Gear Nation.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.040
Tell me what you want, and I
will do anything to help you.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.580
We are searching...

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:53.580
What the hell are you doing?!

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.660
Shing! Disciplining them.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.500
We can't have slaves speaking
on behalf of themselves like that.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.200
U-Um, <i>our master </i>is searching
for this individual.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.410
You're looking for a
living creature? How curious.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:08.450
Something wrong with that?

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.200
Issue a proclamation throughout the land.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.040
Yes, sir.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:17.160
Shing! Until we hear anything,
you are free to stay at my castle.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.540
This is the clam-producing area?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.160
It really isn't doing well, is it?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.950
Of course not! This is a mecha planet!
Nobody eats them! They're all exported!

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.160
Who was it that brought us to this planet?

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.620
Ah, but they do have a grilled clam shop.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.370
Hey! Two orders of grilled clams!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.120
Would you like them gift wrapped?

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.620
No, we're going to eat them.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.790
Huh? Humans?

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:08.910
In human form, we get discriminated
against by mecha-people.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.500
--Yummy!
--Yummy!

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.950
Glad to hear it.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.040
You know,

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.580
that kind of work is the sort that
robots were made for, isn't it?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.120
You're being awfully
discriminatory toward robots!

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:31.160
Shut up! <i>We're </i>the ones
being discriminated against!

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:34.040
They don't work.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.410
Then, what do they do?

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.910
Fight.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:42.040
There are some mecha-feudal lords
who wage war on a battlefield,

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.250
called Se-Mecha-Hara, over and over.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.370
They don't, as a rule, die,
so they fight for the fun of it.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.870
But even mecha-people are finished if
their central processors get destroyed.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:55.540
They follow rules to make sure
they're never completely destroyed.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.080
It's called the "Tao of Mecha," and they
don't use beam weapons or missiles.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.870
So it's bare-knuckle--or rather,
bare-mecha fighting?

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.500
So long as their core data is unharmed,

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.080
they can switch out their bodies
as much as they need to.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:11.700
We work to pay for the bodies
they destroy when they play.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.330
The longer I chew them,
the saltier they taste, huh?

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.950
It's like the taste of sorrow,
or tears, or something.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.750
On the house. They'll just
take it away, anyhow.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:23.540
What's your name, kid?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.290
Hoshiro.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:30.250
Okay, Hoshiro, we'll help you
out a bit, by way of thanks.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.290
Thank you! That's very helpful!

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.410
Hey, it's nothing, really.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:57.000
The king of the mechanical world!
His name is the exalted Chamechamecha!

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.540
The king of the mechanical world...

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.870
So he's the feudal lord over these parts?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.040
Seems so.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.830
You there, mecha-person! Who gave
you permission to harvest clams?

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:10.160
If you are a thief, you will pay for this.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.620
Whrr-whrr-whrr!

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.500
If that's how they want it...

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.120
--Hizakuri Javelin!
--Hizakuri Javelin!

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.330
What do we do now?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.000
No choice but to fight.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.410
In this empty shell of a robot?

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:32.450
"Pray at the Isekandar Temple"

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.410
"Pray at the Isekandar Temple"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:38.450
"Go shopping on Okage Street"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:42.040
"Get Akafucrystals as gifts"
♪ Isekan is a great place! ♪

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.950
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.450
"Act now and this Isekandar bag is included!!"
♪ Come on, let's go! ♪

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:59.500
Hey, come on, I was just
helping with the clam harvesting.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:06.410
Hmph. Come any closer, and my
Hizakuri Javelin will shoot fire!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.950
I mean it! I'll really do it!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.750
Stop!

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.790
Huh?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:24.160
I see you are quite skilled.
I can tell. After all, I am the king.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.700
Whew, sounds like we're safe.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.910
The king must really be blind.

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:33.790
Hmm, would you mind doing
a spot of work for your king?

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.660
What's the spot of work?

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.120
There is a battle with the Mecha-Count
of the neighboring land soon.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:43.040
I would like you to assist
my side in the fighting.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:45.120
The assistance pays 1,000,000 mons!

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:46.370
A million?!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.330
If you win, I'll double that! Boom!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.500
Double?! Boom?!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.000
Two million!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.000
Hey, what do we do?!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.450
Accept! Fight!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.040
I don't want to fight for this guy.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:01.000
Besides, Hizakuriger is a
look-but-don't-touch empty suit.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.040
You heard what that kid said earlier, right?

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.870
They follow the Tao of Mecha, so no
modern weapons! Nobody's gonna die!

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:11.540
We pocket the million mons, and if
it gets too crazy, we'll just scram!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:12.700
Well?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.080
Okay, you got it.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.160
Hmm!

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.540
Come to my palace!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:22.330
Whrr, whrr, whrr. Even on boats,
we whrr, whrr, whrr.

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.080
Okay, we're here!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.500
As far as weapons, we have
drills, tomahawks, yo-yos,

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.660
and all sorts of other things!
Feel free to choose what you like.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:43.580
Oh, I already have my own.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.410
You have modern weapons, too?

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:50.540
Those are for defending our world.
We don't use them in our "wars."

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:52.450
Chame! Chame! Chame!

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:56.120
That is my son, Prince Chamechamecha.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:58.450
He's the prince of this place?

00:13:58.450 --> 00:13:59.870
Does that mean he's blood-related?

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.540
It means they share the same core data!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:07.370
I've prepared a room for you. Feel free
to use it as you see fit while here.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:12.250
Incidentally, I never caught
your name. What do I call you?

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.950
You may call me Hizakuri Sanjuro.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.250
He says he got a room ready for us...

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.750
...but there's no way this
isn't just a regular hangar.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.790
I don't suppose this means there's
a toilet or a bathroom, does it?

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.410
Robots don't use them!

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:28.410
I guess not.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.160
They'll fix us something to eat, though, right?

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:31.870
Do you think that mechas eat?

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:35.660
We could make like we're artificial
lifeforms. Get our fatima on.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:39.290
That might fly for me,
but you'd be out of luck.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:43.950
How mean! Aw, now that I know there
isn't a toilet, I really need one!

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:46.000
I told you, we don't use them!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.580
Damn it! Oh, but there <i>are </i>humans here.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.870
Over there!

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.660
Make way! Make way! There's a robot here!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.790
You're getting carried away now.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:04.120
I need you to share some
of your food with my slaves.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:05.870
Huh? It's you guys?

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:09.200
--Hoshiro? This is where you live?
--H-Hurry... toilet...

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:12.540
Whatever! I just need a toilet, fast!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:19.870
Damn it, why should I have to eat
something as nasty as this?

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.910
Normally, when you invite someone over,
you throw them a banquet!

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.910
It's because mechas don't eat food.

00:15:24.910 --> 00:15:27.620
This is all they have for us humans.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.700
Damn it! What kind of world is this?!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.330
The clam broth does add a nice flavor,

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.910
but when your other ingredient
is silkworm cocoons...

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.830
Everything the estate harvests is exported,

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.370
so this is all that's left for us.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:46.830
Ugh. If it were me, I'd start a revolution.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.790
Revolution?

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:53.870
Yeah! A popular uprising! Overthrow
the power! You aren't familiar?

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.080
No, I'm not.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:58.910
Yeah, being born on this
godforsaken world, you wouldn't be.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.250
Yeah, there's nothing I can do.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:05.910
I, too, thought that no matter
what I did, my life wouldn't change.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:09.910
But then someone said to me, if you
live your life on arrow-straight rails,

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:12.120
it will never change.

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:13.580
Rails?

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.500
Yes. If you don't turn and bump
into things on either side,

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.950
nothing unpredictable will
ever happen to you.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:22.540
I don't know who that guy was,
but that's some good stuff.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:28.160
Tell me! How can I bend my rails?!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.410
Listen up. The fight begins
at the break of dawn.

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.500
Hey, what happened to your
promise to find Robby?

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.870
I still haven't found him.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.500
Enough! We'll find him ourselves!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:46.040
Ka-shing! Do not forget that
you are my defender!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:50.870
Tch! I don't even understand
what you're fighting about!

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.950
Our fighting is a chance to prove
our level of performance!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.410
It is our noble sport!

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.750
It's a game?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.910
No, our very lives at stake.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:05.040
Our fighting provides the natural selection
mecha-people need to evolve.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.620
Yahoo! To war! Let's go to Se-Mecha-Hara!

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:16.040
Chamechamecha!

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.500
These guys really love their fighting.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.450
We got our advance pay. What do we do?

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:23.120
For now, we head out with them, and pretend.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.540
If the chance comes along, we whoop
some ass. We beat it after that.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.290
Off to Se-Mecha-Hara!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.450
"East: The Mecha-Count's Forces!"

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.660
"West: King Chamechamecha's Forces!"

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.700
Wait, what is this?!

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:54.410
Damn that Count! He's dispersed
Minovsky particles!

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:57.290
Our camera eyes have been jammed,
and our visibility is poor!

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.330
Damn it, I can't see anything!

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.750
However, the Count is under the
same conditions. Forward, men!

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:06.200
Chamechamecha!

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:12.540
Shing!

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:14.750
Let's go, men!

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.450
Wah! There's no way!

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.330
We really are in the flesh, here!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:23.580
Silence! Be quiet and keep moving!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.750
It's no use. There's too much noise to see.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.250
Hatchi, open the hatch
and use your own eyes!

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.750
There, we can see, right?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.870
There's still too much noise for me to see.

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:43.700
That's because your camera
eyes are being jammed.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:47.660
This group relies too heavily
on electronic devices.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.450
We can do whatever we want, then!

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.000
Hizakuri Javelin!

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.620
Hizakuri Javelin!

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.540
Hizakuri-kuri-kuri Javelin!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.330
Hiza-Hiza-Hizakuri Javelin!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.830
Hiza-k-k-k-kuri Javelin!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.540
Hiza-Hiza-Hiza

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.790
kuri-kuri-kuri Ja-Javelin!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.910
King's Drill!

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:17.500
Master Hizakuriger is distinguishing himself!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:21.330
I should have known. Let's seize this
momentum and defeat the Count!

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.200
Right!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.500
--Whrr!
--Vroom!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.160
--Whrr!
--Vroom-vroom-vroom!

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.750
--Whrr-whrr-whrr!
--Vroom!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.540
Chame!

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:43.250
They're taking this too far,
just because we're mecha. Shing!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:46.750
Why, you...!

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.870
I'm going to kill you!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:55.040
"What is it to be human, anyway?"

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.540
Huh?

00:19:56.540 --> 00:20:00.080
That guy's pretty small, huh? Piece of cake!

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:04.000
He snuck in close!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.330
Stomp on him!

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.950
All of these mechas suffer
from the same weakness.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:18.700
Way to go, Mr. Yang!

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.540
You're Yang? But how--?

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:23.250
You're not getting away this time, Robby.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:25.830
I told you we should have fled earlier.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:26.950
Whoa, hold on!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:32.290
On this planet, humans are slaves.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.620
Now what is it?!

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:42.790
What was that?!

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:44.790
Shing! What's going on?!

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.910
My son!

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:50.830
Curse you! You've violated the rules!

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.370
No, <i>you </i>have!

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.540
It's a revolution!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.330
A revolution?!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.750
Shing!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.910
Are you okay, guys?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.330
Yeah. Thanks to you guys, we're fine.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:20.250
Hoshiro, you've bent your rails, huh?

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.700
Mm-hmm!

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:23.330
You guys get on out of here.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:26.080
You'll be caught in the middle
of the revolution inside that robot.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.540
Then we won't hesitate.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:29.950
Later!

00:21:29.950 --> 00:21:31.080
Be safe!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.290
Imagine, them actually starting a revolution!

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.080
All thanks to you, right?

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.660
Huh? How so?

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:47.080
Whew, at last the jamming is gone.
What a nightmare that was--

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.200
I could say the same!

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.620
You try something like that again,
and I'll disassemble you!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:55.830
Yes indeed. Robots were originally
created for people, after all--

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.910
as partners.

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:00.450
So then treat me right, as a partner!

00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:02.700
Okay, let's head off toward
the next stage station world!

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:05.290
Yeah, we've gotta give
Yang the slip, or we're--

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.080
He's not coming after us, is he?

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:14.160
Mister, why are you helping us?

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:17.330
Because I do not like these mecha bastards.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.830
Revolution!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:53.000
"Next time"
"#09 'The Family That Sticks Together, Hizakuriger'"

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:57.160
"Next time"
"#09 'The Family That Sticks Together, Hizakuriger'"
Next time, "The Family That
Sticks Together, Hizakuriger."

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:01.870
"The industrial planet Yokkamarché,"
"the world where Hizakuriger
was manufactured"

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:06.910
"At last, the secret of
Hizakuriger is revealed!"
"It all started 50 years ago"
